  "about": "Reactions to direct messages (canvas home/conversation; the web's dm.ts). A reaction is an unsigned kind 7 rumor, content = the emoji, tags [\"e\", <the kind 14 rumor's id>, \"\", <its author>], [\"p\", <its author>], [\"k\", \"14\"], then [\"p\", …] for the other participants, gift-wrapped (NIP-59) to every participant and to yourself. Taking it back: a kind 5 rumor [\"e\", <the reaction rumor's id>], [\"k\", \"7\"], [\"p\", …] for the others, wrapped the same way; it counts only from the reaction's author, and also when it is read before the reaction. Readers key on the last e tag; one per person per emoji; \"+\" or empty = 👍; more than 16 UTF-16 units = ignored. chips: by count, most first (ties: first given first); who in the order they first gave it; mine = the viewer gave it. Never on e-mail (1301).",
